[node name="Borders" type="Node2D" parent="." unique_id=781993619]
editor_description = "Borders, as lines along the edges the counties share: the lesser first, so that a greater is drawn over it. A border that reaches the coast runs on a little into the coast's line. Water and roads are drawn over the borders. So where a border runs along a river, a lake's shore or a road, a second line (named Along...) lies under that river, shore or road, wide enough to show the border's colour on both sides of it."

[node name="Counties" type="Node2D" parent="Borders" unique_id=1411110969]

